17	 * {@code PENDING} against an empty ledger — which is a Transfer nothing will ever settle,
18	 * expire or explain, holding an operator's funds until somebody notices. {@link
19	 * Propagation#MANDATORY} is that requirement stated to the container rather than left as a
20	 * convention for the caller to honour: this method cannot start a transaction of its own,
21	 * so the only way to call it is from inside one that is already writing the Transfer.
22	 *
23	 * <p>Being late is one way to that state and requiring nothing is the other: a policy that
24	 * names no Check makes {@link #openFor} write no rows and return, so the caller commits the
25	 * same stuck Transfer with every test still green. The refusal below is that second way
26	 * closed, at the only place that can see it happening.
27	 *
28	 * <p>The method is public on a package-private-by-default design because {@code
29	 * @Transactional} on a non-public method is silently ignored under proxy-based AOP — the
30	 * trap {@link hu.bankmonitor.payments} documents. The class is public for the ordinary
31	 * reason: {@code FundsReservation} is in the parent package and has to name it.
32	 */
